"""E57 job 1280 (recompute oracle): LIGHT pilot-informed registration text, v10 (server repo copy; DRAFT; text only, no new .md file). Analysis code: e57_1280_analyze.py. Timing evidence = the public commit hash of this file and of the analysis script that precede the first confirmatory output. DELETED from earlier versions: the A / B / A-prime hash freezes, the external timestamp, the predictive-probability futility rule, the interim look and its boundaries, the blind failure-classification procedure. Nothing in this text was written after opening any 1280, instrumentation or auxiliary-seed output (none exists)."""
import re
PLACEHOLDERS=['SESOI_fact / SESOI_token values (from the auxiliary measurement 901..908; needs Hans GPU sentence; c = .5 is fixed here)','instrumentation k (from seeds 91..94; needs Hans GPU sentence)']
REGISTRATION_V10=r"""1 STATUS AND TERMS. This is a PILOT-INFORMED registered analysis: the thresholds were fixed after the 3-seed pilot (job 1279), see item 11. Unqualified pre-registration wording is not used; the term is 'pilot-informed registered analysis'. A non-significant result is NOT evidence that there is no leak. Timing evidence is the public commit hash of this text and of e57_1280_analyze.py, committed before the first confirmatory output exists (check_commit_precedes_results).
2 DESIGN. n = 30 confirmatory seeds (101..130), one fixed-sample analysis; no interim look, no stopping, no extension; unit = seed. Instrumentation seeds 91..94 (variance components at k = 8 only) and the auxiliary SESOI seeds 901..908 are separate from the confirmatory seeds and never enter them. Every arm and every seed result is reported.
3 CLAIMS AND GATES (table CLAIMS_TABLE; one-sided, alpha = .05 each; intersection-union hierarchy 3a -> 3b -> 3c, size <= .05). E-form: E = NLL(blocked) - NLL(not blocked); E_cache = a - nc, E_rec = b - c, E_mask = recomputed band NLL - recomputed natural NLL (nat/token); margins G = M_NATMASK - M_NATS, H = M_RECOMP - M_NATS (nat/fact). Contrasts T_R = E_cache - .8 E_rec, T_Q = E_rec - .7 E_mask, L_F = H - .7 G; placebo: PLd = M_RECOMP_PL - M_NATS with one-sided upper confidence bound < delta_PL = .25 nat (absolute). Gates 2a (E_rec > 0, mean >= .25), 2b (E_mask > 0, mean >= .10), 2c (G > 0). Verdict 4 CACHE SUFFICIENT = gate 2a and T_R > 0, a separate claim at its own .05. Flags (not claims): F_LOW, H_GEN, HALF_PL, ANOMALY, G_PRACTICAL. Individual components (T_R leak, T_Q, L_F, placebo) are reported Holm-adjusted over the four tests; a component without a Holm-adjusted rejection outside the intersection claim is labelled EXPLORATORY.
4 TESTS AND WORDING. Each test is run twice: the seed-paired t test (df = 29) and the exact sign-flip test (all 2^30 sign vectors, exact under symmetry of the seed contrast about 0 under H0). 'Significant' is written only when BOTH reject. When the t test rejects and the exact test does not, the wording is 'supported, distribution-sensitive'. When only the exact test rejects there is no claim (flag SIGNFLIP_ONLY). The wording of every outcome is drafted in OUTCOME_PHRASES before the results exist.
5 SEEDS AND FAILURES. A failure is a seed whose run diverges or yields a non-finite value. At most 3 failed seeds are replaced, in order, by 131, 132, 133; every failure is reported with its seed and kind; beyond the cap the analysis uses the remaining seeds and reports n. A failure is never classified by its outcome (fill_seeds raises on any other reason).
6 SESOI. SESOI_x = c * (mean K0 = 0 NATS 16->128 gain in unit x), c = .5, fixed here BEFORE the auxiliary seeds 901..908 are opened. Written rationale: a leak-related effect is treated as practically relevant only if it is at least half of what the standard write procedure gains over the 16 -> 128 exposure ladder (three doublings of exposure); .5 is the conventional half-effect anchor; .25 and 1.0 are shown as sensitivity only. nat/fact (margin gain per fact) and nat/token (NLL gain per later-exposure fact token) are measured separately, never converted. An unstable measurement (valid seeds < 6 of 8, CI lower <= 0, half-width > .5 * mean) falls back to .5 nat/fact; nat/token is then undefined. SESOI enters no test; it defines the flag G_PRACTICAL (lower bound of G > SESOI_fact). delta_PL = .25 nat absolute.
7 CONFOUND TABLE (CONFOUND_TABLE): placebo and oracle arms are matched in masked length (exactly), position (mean masked position within 64 tokens) and checked for attention mass; attention mass is NOT matched and is reported as a covariate per seed (confound_check); a length or position mismatch is reported with the seed.
8 GENERALITY BRIDGE (one candidate, BRIDGE_CANDIDATE): public-QA write stream NATS vs NATMASK, exploratory, not part of the 3c claim.
9 POWER AND GPU TIME AT n = 30: see POWER_NOTE (grid margin SD x rho(G,H); t only and t-and-exact; numbers in e57_1280_power_n30.json; GPU hours in GPU_NOTE; values >= .9999 are printed '>=.9999'; no claim of achieving a power target is made).
10 1284 IS A SEPARATE FAMILY: seeds 201..220, its own alpha = .05 one-sided, primary RECOMP-ORACLE - RECOMP-PL, key secondary HALF-PL - HALF; it is not pooled with 1280 and shares no seed (checked).
11 DISCLOSURE. Pilot (job 1279, seeds 62..64, K0 = 0, exploratory, 2 degrees of freedom, excluded from the confirmatory set): X_ORACLE .076 / .065 / .079; X_MASK .337 / .367 / .383; PLACEBO - NATS +.096 / +.036 / -.003; RAND - NATS +.048 / -.010 / -.022. Thresholds fixed after the pilot: .25, .10, .8, .7, .7, .3, .5 (SESOI coefficient and fallback), 1.2, 3 of 32 unmatched, delta_PL .25, n = 30, the cap of 3 replacements. Expectation (not a prediction): E_cache is small relative to E_rec (pilot .07 vs .36), so if gate 2a passes the leak direction follows almost automatically; the T_R leak result is therefore not counted as independent confirmation. Power statements are scenario estimates.
12 DELETED FROM EARLIER VERSIONS: A / B / A-prime hash freezes, external timestamp, predictive-probability futility, interim look and boundaries, blind failure classification, informative-failure sensitivity, SESOI estimator options. Archived in git (commits up to 1fdb266472fb9270b269279b3640b3ddbc037c46)."""
CLAIMS_TABLE=[
 dict(id='gate 2a',claim='the recomputed blocking effect E_rec is certified',estimand='E_rec (nat/token)',test='t and exact sign-flip, one-sided; mean >= .25',level=.05,gate='-',if_significant='E_rec is certified'),
 dict(id='gate 2b',claim='the recomputed band effect E_mask is certified',estimand='E_mask (nat/token)',test='t and exact, one-sided; mean >= .10',level=.05,gate='2a',if_significant='E_mask is certified'),
 dict(id='gate 2c',claim='the masked update has a positive margin effect G',estimand='G (nat/fact)',test='t and exact, one-sided',level=.05,gate='2a',if_significant='G > 0'),
 dict(id='3a',claim='the cached oracle explains less than 80% of the recomputed effect (leak)',estimand='T_R = E_cache - .8 E_rec < 0',test='t and exact, one-sided',level=.05,gate='2a',if_significant='R-leak'),
 dict(id='3b',claim='3a and the recomputed band effect explains the recomputed oracle effect',estimand='T_Q = E_rec - .7 E_mask > 0',test='t and exact, one-sided',level=.05,gate='2a, 2b, 3a',if_significant='R-leak and Q'),
 dict(id='3c',claim='3b and the margin effect follows the masked direction, and the placebo does not exceed .25 nat',estimand='L_F = H - .7 G > 0; PLd upper bound < .25',test='t and exact, one-sided',level=.05,gate='2a, 2b, 2c, 3b',if_significant='leak confirmed'),
 dict(id='4',claim='the cached oracle is sufficient',estimand='T_R = E_cache - .8 E_rec > 0',test='t and exact, one-sided',level=.05,gate='2a',if_significant='cache sufficient')]
CONFOUND_TABLE=[
 dict(arm_pair='ORACLE (cached) vs ORACLE-PL',masked='earlier same-fact sentences (oracle) vs other facts sentences (placebo)',length='masked token count equal (exact)',position='mean masked position within 64 tokens',attention_mass='reported covariate, not matched',check='confound_check'),
 dict(arm_pair='RECOMP vs RECOMP-PL',masked='recomputed oracle band vs recomputed placebo band',length='masked token count equal (exact)',position='mean masked position within 64 tokens',attention_mass='reported covariate, not matched',check='confound_check'),
 dict(arm_pair='HALF vs HALF-PL',masked='band-256 half oracle (own-fact exposures reopened) vs its placebo',length='masked token count equal (exact)',position='mean masked position within 64 tokens',attention_mass='reported covariate, not matched',check='confound_check')]
BRIDGE_CANDIDATE=dict(name='public-QA write stream, NATS vs NATMASK (e57_pqa_natmask_run.py)',question='does the masked-direction update effect G found in the synthetic fact worlds also appear on public-QA facts',contrast='G_QA = margin(NATMASK) - margin(NATS) per bundle, one-sided',unit='bundle (5 bundles, 65-version stream); EXPLORATORY: reported with CI, no claim',gpu_time='about 2 h (measured: write job 1268 took 107 min for 5 arms, so about 45 min for 2 arms; read stage about 80 min as in job 1295; to be re-measured)',status='design only; needs Hans GPU sentence')
OUTCOME_PHRASES={
 '3c':"In this pilot-informed registered analysis (n = {n} seeds), blocking the earlier same-fact exposure from the update path raised the later-exposure NLL by {E_rec:.3f} nat/token under full recomputation, whereas the cached oracle accounted for only {E_cache:.3f} nat/token (T_R = {TR:.3f}); both the t test and the exact sign-flip test rejected at the one-sided .05 level for every step of the hierarchy, including the margin effect (G = {G:.2f} nat/fact) and the placebo bound (< .25 nat).",
 '3b':"In this pilot-informed registered analysis (n = {n} seeds), the cached oracle under-explained the recomputed blocking effect (T_R = {TR:.3f}) and the recomputed band effect explained it (T_Q), with both the t test and the exact sign-flip test rejecting; the margin and placebo conditions of the full claim were not both met, so we report the leak mechanism without the margin-level confirmation.",
 '3a':"In this pilot-informed registered analysis (n = {n} seeds), the cached oracle explained less than 80% of the recomputed blocking effect (T_R = {TR:.3f}; t and exact sign-flip both rejected); the band-effect step did not reach significance, which is not evidence that the band effect is absent.",
 '4':"In this pilot-informed registered analysis (n = {n} seeds), the cached oracle accounted for at least 80% of the recomputed blocking effect (T_R = {TR:.3f}; t and exact sign-flip both rejected), so the stale-cache account is sufficient for this setting.",
 '2a':"In this pilot-informed registered analysis (n = {n} seeds), the recomputed blocking effect was not certified above .25 nat/token (E_rec = {E_rec:.3f}); the downstream comparisons are therefore not interpreted, and this does not establish that there is no leak.",
 '6':"In this pilot-informed registered analysis (n = {n} seeds), no step of the leak hierarchy was significant under both tests; a non-significant result is not evidence of the absence of a leak, and the effect sizes with their intervals are reported in full.",
 'sensitive':"The {level} result is supported by the t test but not by the exact sign-flip test (supported, distribution-sensitive); we therefore do not describe it as significant.",
 '1':"The protocol or instrument checks failed in this pilot-informed registered analysis, so the results are reported as exploratory only."}
TERM_RULES=['use "pilot-informed"; never an unqualified "pre-registered"','never write that a non-significant result shows there is no leak','"significant" only when both the t test and the exact sign-flip test reject; otherwise "supported, distribution-sensitive"']
def check_terms(text):
    """returns the list of violations of TERM_RULES in text ('pre-registered' without 'pilot-informed ' directly before it; 'no leak' sentences without a negation; 'non-significant' / 'not significant' sentences without 'not evidence' or 'does not establish')"""
    v=[]
    if re.search(r'(?i)(?<!pilot-informed )pre-?registered',text):v.append('unqualified pre-registered')
    for sent in re.split(r'(?<=[.;])\s+',text):
        low=sent.lower()
        if re.search(r'\bno leak(age)?\b',low) and not re.search(r"\bnot\b|\bn't\b",low):v.append('no-leak claim: '+sent[:60])
        if re.search(r'non-?significant|not significant',low) and not re.search(r'not evidence|does not establish|not evidence of',low):v.append('non-significance without caveat: '+sent[:60])
    return v
POWER_NOTE='fixed n = 30, one-sided .05 per test, scenario E_cache .07, E_rec .30, E_mask .35, G 2.0, H 1.6, PLd 0 (delta_PL .25), margin SD {.225, .45, .90} x rho(G,H) {0, .7, .9}, N = 1e5 common random numbers (t only) and the first 1e4 with the exact sign-flip test; marginal power per component, joint, product of marginals, Frechet bounds. Result (joint 3c power, t only / t and exact): margin SD .225: .987, >=.9999, >=.9999 (rho 0, .7, .9); SD .45: .559, .864, .907 (t and exact .558, .862, .905); SD .90: .110, .221, .348 (t and exact .114, .224, .345); bottleneck components F (L_F) and PL (placebo); joint minus product of marginals within .001 in every cell. For comparison the former n = 20 design gave .351, .644, .758 at SD .45'
GPU_NOTE='GPU hours = seeds x minutes per seed; per-seed minutes are NOT measured for the 1280 branch arms: optimistic 45 / central 60 / pessimistic 90 give 22.5 / 30 / 45 h for n = 30 (15 / 20 / 30 h for the former n = 20); the auxiliary seeds 901..908 (NATS only, about 10 min per arm, about 1.5 h) and the instrumentation seeds 91..94 (4 seeds at k = 8, about 4 h at the central estimate) are extra; the runner benchmark is pending'
def selftest():
    import e57_1280_analyze as A
    assert REGISTRATION_V10.count('\n')==11 and 'pilot-informed' in REGISTRATION_V10 and 'Archived in git' in REGISTRATION_V10
    assert check_terms(REGISTRATION_V10)==[],check_terms(REGISTRATION_V10)
    for k,t in OUTCOME_PHRASES.items():
        bad=check_terms(t);assert not bad,(k,bad)
    assert set(OUTCOME_PHRASES)=={'3c','3b','3a','4','2a','6','sensitive','1'}
    labels=[ '3c','3b','3a','4','2a','6','1']
    for ph in labels:assert ph in OUTCOME_PHRASES
    assert check_terms('The effect was pre-registered.')==['unqualified pre-registered'] and check_terms('This shows there is no leak.') and check_terms('The result was not significant.') and not check_terms('The result was not significant, which is not evidence of no leak.')
    assert not check_terms('This is a pilot-informed pre-registered analysis.')
    assert [r['id'] for r in CLAIMS_TABLE]==['gate 2a','gate 2b','gate 2c','3a','3b','3c','4'] and all(r['level']==0.05 for r in CLAIMS_TABLE)
    assert len(CONFOUND_TABLE)==3 and all('confound_check' in r['check'] for r in CONFOUND_TABLE)
    assert A.P['delta_PL_value']==0.25 and A.P['sesoi_coef']==0.5 and A.SEEDS_1284[0]==201
    fm=OUTCOME_PHRASES['3c'].format(n=30,E_rec=0.3,E_cache=0.07,TR=-0.17,G=2.0);assert 'pilot-informed' in fm and not check_terms(fm)
    print('e57_1280_registration selftest ok')
if __name__=='__main__':
    import sys
    if '--selftest' in sys.argv:selftest()
